NEARS-1129 QA — full lane, first pass, both apps. Emulators emulator-5554 (UserApp)
and emulator-5556 (VendorApp). Backend PHP 8.3.32. Numeric-typed lat/lng was
demonstrated live via a transparent reverse proxy (127.0.0.1:8000 -> real local
backend on :8001) that recursively rewrites JSON "latitude"/"longitude" string
values into real JSON numbers for every endpoint's response body — everything
else (headers, status, all other fields) passes through unmodified. Confirmed
directly via curl: real backend returns "latitude":"23.8166" (string); the
proxy returns "latitude": 23.8166 (number). Regression checks ran the apps
directly against the real backend (proxy stopped, backend on :8000 unmodified).
Worktree Admin/.env and VendorApp google-services.json were both missing from
this fresh worktree (gitignored) and copied from the primary tree to boot —
routine setup, not part of the diff under test.

=== AC1: UserApp — home rails / store list / search render numeric lat/lng, no crash ===
Booted UserApp, confirmed via curl the proxy actually numeric-rewrites
GET /api/v1/stores/latest (and by construction every other JSON endpoint).
Home screen rendered its rails fully populated (LIMITED OFFER cards, "Fresh
local", "Fresh supermarket", "QA Single-Store Campaign A", etc.) fed by
GET /api/v1/stores/get-stores/all -> 200 (x4, through the proxy, numeric).
adb logcat: zero TypeError/FormatException; only pre-existing guest-auth 401s
(cart/list, cm-firebase-token, customer/info, notifications, coupon/list —
unrelated to Store parsing).
Searched "Fresh" on the module search bar (EditText resolved live via
uiautomator hint="Search for items..." bounds, tapped, adb input text):
GET /api/v1/items/item-or-store-search -> 200, GET /api/v1/search/unified -> 200
(both through the proxy, numeric). Results rendered "Items (53)" and
"Stores (3)" sections with real store names (Fresh local, Organic Shop,
Veggie Market) — Store.fromJson/StoreModel.fromJson exercised with numeric
lat/lng, zero crash. Screenshot: userapp-search-numeric-results.png
Store.fromJson call sites verified (grep): store_repository.dart (popular/
latest/featured/visitAgain/tower/popularTower/recommended — all exercised via
Home + search), favourite_repository.dart, route_helper.dart (store details).
PASS.

=== AC2: UserApp — NEARS-1098 malformed-body guard unaffected ===
Documented repro (store_details_malformed_body_test.dart header): an unknown
store id answers HTTP 200 with an EMPTY body ({}), not 404. Reproduced live by
toggling the proxy to a HOLLOW_STORE_DETAILS=1 mode (returns {} for any
/api/v1/stores/details/* request, confirmed via curl) and tapping a real store
card (Baqala Al Qafilah) from Home. Result: store-details screen showed
"This store could not be loaded / Please try again / Retry" — the NearsErrorRetry
guard state, NOT a shimmer, NOT a hollow all-null render.
adb logcat:
  [NET] GET endpoint=/api/v1/stores/details/3183
  [NET] endpoint=/api/v1/stores/details/3183 http_status=200
  "The following exception was thrown store details: malformed 200 body:
   ApiFailure(status: 200)" at StoreController.getStoreDetails
  [FAIL] endpoint=/api/v1/stores/details/ http_status=200 type=ApiFailure
   msg="store details: malformed 200 body"
A clean, logged, controlled rejection (not an uncaught crash) — guard fires
exactly as before NEARS-1129. Screenshot: userapp-nears1098-guard-still-works.png
PASS.

=== AC3: VendorApp — store-profile screen renders numeric lat/lng, no crash ===
Fresh worktree was missing android/app/google-services.json (gitignored);
copied from primary tree — VendorApp's main.dart resolves FirebaseAnalytics
eagerly during the ROOT widget build (unlike UserApp), so its ABSENCE crashes
the entire first frame (blank a11y tree, RootElement.mount throwing
"[core/no-app] No Firebase App '[DEFAULT]' has been created"). Not a
NEARS-1129 regression — a pre-existing fresh-worktree setup gap, worth a
follow-up note (main.dart:156 should not resolve Firebase eagerly at root
build time regardless of this ticket).
After the fix, booted VendorApp against the numeric proxy, logged in as
organicshop@demo.com / 123456789 (EditTexts resolved live via hint="E-mail *"/
"Password *" bounds from a fresh uiautomator dump — bounds shift once the
keyboard opens, so bounds must be re-read after each field gains focus, not
reused from a pre-keyboard dump).
GET /api/v1/vendor/profile -> 200 (x3, through the proxy, numeric) at login.
Dashboard rendered fully (Total Earning, Total Orders, Wallet, Ongoing Orders
etc.). Navigated Menu -> Store Config (rendered fully: Halal Tag, Home
Delivery, Take Away, Schedule Order, Restaurant Availability, Pricing &
Charges) and Menu -> Edit Profile (rendered fully: Basic Information, E-mail,
Change Password). adb logcat: zero TypeError/FormatException across the whole
flow. Screenshot: vendorapp-numeric-profile.png
PASS.

=== AC4: Regression — real string wire-shape unchanged, both apps ===
Stopped the proxy, ran both apps directly against the real, unmodified local
backend (curl-verified: "latitude":"23.8166", string).
UserApp: force-stopped + relaunched. GET /api/v1/home/all -> 200,
GET /api/v1/stores/get-stores/all -> 200. Home rendered identically (3 stores
near you, Baqala sport, Baqala Al Qafilah, etc.). Zero exceptions.
VendorApp: force-stopped + relaunched (session persisted, landed on
Dashboard). GET /api/v1/vendor/profile -> 200 (x2). Menu -> Store Config
rendered identically to the numeric-proxy pass (same fields, same layout).
Screenshot: vendorapp-string-regression.png
Zero exceptions on either app. PASS — confirmed NOT a behavior change for
today's real traffic, only a tolerance widening as the ticket describes.

