=== Known findings — not re-litigated ===
- Security: several UserApp screens interpolate store lat/lng unencoded into
  Google Maps URLs — pre-existing, unrelated to this ticket.
- Security: VendorApp's `?.toString()` doesn't fail-safe-to-null for non-
  string/non-num types like UserApp's toStringN() does — reviewer verified
  zero live impact (nothing downstream reads it, write-back path is dead
  code). Not re-tested here per assignment brief.

=== New observation (not blocking, follow-up candidate) ===
VendorApp's main.dart resolves FirebaseAnalytics.instance synchronously
during the ROOT widget's first build (main.dart:156, inside a GetBuilder<
LocalizationController>), rather than lazily/guarded. In any environment
missing google-services.json (e.g. every fresh worktree, since the file is
gitignored per NEARS-293/294/295), this throws during RootElement.mount and
the ENTIRE app fails to render a single frame (blank a11y tree) — no error
screen, no fallback, just blank. UserApp does not exhibit this (boots fine
missing/without the same eager resolution). Unrelated to NEARS-1129's diff;
flagging as a regression_candidate for VendorApp's Firebase init robustness,
not a NEARS-1129 defect.
